WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:04.240
(sirens ring)

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:06.960
- When you roll up to that line,

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.140
you are getting butterflies
in your stomach,

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.220
you're nervous, you're sweating

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.309
but once you get the bug, you get hooked

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:16.811
and then it's all over.

00:00:16.811 --> 00:00:19.394
(upbeat music)

00:00:22.861 --> 00:00:24.890
We're celebrating our 23rd year

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:29.057
of the Top the Cop Program
here at Sonoma Raceway.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.756
Top the Cops is a program

00:00:31.756 --> 00:00:35.406
where high school students
can come out to the race track

00:00:35.406 --> 00:00:37.019
on a Wednesday night,

00:00:37.019 --> 00:00:40.477
race their car against
a uniformed policeman

00:00:40.477 --> 00:00:42.310
in a stock police car.

00:00:43.365 --> 00:00:45.237
I'm Kevin McKinnie, the program director

00:00:45.237 --> 00:00:47.325
for the Top the Cops Program.

00:00:47.325 --> 00:00:49.383
I'm a retired law enforcement officer

00:00:49.383 --> 00:00:51.591
from the Santa Rosa Police Department.

00:00:51.591 --> 00:00:54.322
We've been doing this
from April through August

00:00:54.322 --> 00:00:56.322
for the past 23 seasons.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:59.271
(car engine roars)

00:00:59.271 --> 00:01:02.482
There was illegal street
racing being done in

00:01:02.482 --> 00:01:04.722
and around the city of Santa Rosa,

00:01:04.722 --> 00:01:09.421
and I thought we need to
get these people over here

00:01:09.421 --> 00:01:11.381
to the race track so they stop doing it

00:01:11.381 --> 00:01:13.292
out on the street.

00:01:13.292 --> 00:01:16.111
If you wanna race, fine, come on out here

00:01:16.111 --> 00:01:18.602
and race, don't do it out on the street.

00:01:18.602 --> 00:01:21.519
(car engine roars)

00:01:23.463 --> 00:01:27.033
These are our future, these kids here.

00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:28.934
- When I pull up next to
a cop at the start line

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:31.077
I always just think, “Oh, it'd
be great if I beat them.”

00:01:31.077 --> 00:01:32.735
It's great feeling when you
pass them on the drag shift

00:01:32.735 --> 00:01:34.735
going 100 miles an hour.

00:01:35.886 --> 00:01:38.170
- There is a very competitive spirit to it,

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:40.759
but you know, it's all about the kids.

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:43.461
There's a lot of negativity
in the world today

00:01:43.461 --> 00:01:46.570
and a lot of negativity
towards law enforcement.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:49.119
What we try to do out here

00:01:49.119 --> 00:01:52.270
is make something good, something positive

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:53.341
out of this program,

00:01:53.341 --> 00:01:56.420
something that is worthwhile.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.511
Nowhere in the country is this being done

00:01:58.511 --> 00:02:00.012
on a regular basis.

00:02:00.012 --> 00:02:02.461
The Top the Cops Program did help curb

00:02:02.461 --> 00:02:04.126
illegal street racing.

00:02:04.126 --> 00:02:07.287
It's been a great positive
program all these years.

00:02:07.287 --> 00:02:09.870
(sirens ring)

